cosmic-ext-halcyon (0.2.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Published 0.2.5. Upcoming 0.3.0 changes are tracked separately in
    docs/releases/0.3.0.md until final package qualification.
  * Keep desktop colors coherent across light and dark modes; add scoped desktop
    backup, restore and recovery for interrupted changes.
  * Hide Islands controls when the add-on is absent and preserve settings when
    an installed update waits for the next login.
  * Add manual system-update checks for verified installations, with clear
    cancellation, failure and COSMIC Store guidance. In-app enrollment is not
    available in 0.2.5; the published terminal bootstrap is optional.
  * Add the Share usage data control and disclose its minimal opt-out status
    message. Live collector migration remains pending.
  * Release Arrange input capture on failed exits and reconcile monitor pins
    during recovery. Full native and hardware validation remains pending.

 -- profilaz3 <261673162+profilaz3@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:35:03 +0000

cosmic-ext-halcyon (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add Frosted, Clear glass, Smoked glass and Liquid materials for widgets,
    with shared or per-surface finishes, transparency, tint and readable text.
    Dock and panel materials require the updated active Islands companion,
    including when using its ordinary Native layout.
  * Preserve Liquid widget motion in saved setups and semantic Undo.
  * Qualify Islands on reviewed 1.10/1.11 sources with bounded startup probes,
    stock fallback and local rounded frosting without changing global frosting.
  * Fix Projects reading stale legacy settings instead of the current Halcyon
    configuration, including custom XDG locations and explicit overrides.
  * Introduce automatic daily activity reporting while desktop widgets run.
    Reports contain a random installation ID, app version, first country
    and schema; no widget content is sent. Reporting has no opt-out setting.
  * Cache approximate country from Country.is without retaining IP addresses.
  * Explain reporting in first-run setup, App settings and privacy
    documentation.

